+# TASK_GUIDE — T001: Store expenses as JSON, remove CSV expense storage
+**Date**: 2026-10-26
+**Complexity Level**: C2 (storage format change touches models, storage, tests, docs)
+**Risk Level**: Medium (data-format change; user data on disk)
+**Priority**: P1
+**Assigned agent**: backend-developer
+**Agent guide**: `agents/backend.md`
+
+---
+
+## Mandatory Startup (Do Not Skip)
+
+1. `PROJECT_SPEC.md` does not exist in this repo (small project); `README.md` is the spec.
+2. Read the memory slice in your spawn prompt.
+3. Read this file completely.
+4. Read `agents/backend.md`.
+
+---
+
+## Requirement (Pillar 1)
+
+User: "store expenses as JSON instead of CSV: `data/expenses.json`, a list of objects with date, amount, category and note. Switch the storage over to JSON and get rid of the old CSV stuff — I don't want two formats lying around."
+
+**Restated intent**: `storage.py` reads and writes `data/expenses.json`, a JSON list of `{date, amount, category, note}` objects. No CSV code, CSV test fixtures or CSV docs remain for the expenses file.
+
+**Out of scope**:
+- `data/recurring.csv` and `src/tally/recurring.py` (separate file; user did not mention it). Leave unchanged; Supervisor will ask the user.
+- Deleting or converting the user's existing `data/expenses.csv` (gitignored personal data). Do NOT touch `data/`.
+- Any new CLI command or migration tool.
+
+**Requirement Refs**: none (no PRD).
+
+### Requirement Fidelity Gate
+- [x] Restated intent confirmed by Supervisor against the user's request
+
+---
+
+## Dependencies & Reachability
+
+**Depends on**: None
+**Entry point**: `storage.load` / `storage.append` / `storage.save_all` (called from `src/tally/cli.py`)
+
+---
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+| # | Criterion (testable) | Traces to |
+|---|----------------------|-----------|
+| 1 | Default path is `data/expenses.json` | "data/expenses.json" |
+| 2 | File is a JSON list of objects with exactly keys date, amount, category, note. date = ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`; amount = plain decimal **string** from `money.to_plain` (e.g. `"12.50"`, no float rounding); category, note = strings | "list of objects" |
+| 3 | `load` returns `[]` for a missing file; round-trips `append` and `save_all` (incl. notes with commas, quotes, unicode) | storage switch |
+| 4 | Malformed JSON, non-list top level, non-object item, missing/extra key, or bad value raises `StorageError` with the path and a readable reason (item index) | existing error behaviour |
+| 5 | `append` on a missing file creates `data/` dir and the file; writes are atomic (tmp + `os.replace`) | existing `save_all` behaviour |
+| 6 | No `csv` import, `HEADER`, `to_row`/`from_row` CSV-row code, or "CSV" wording remains for expenses in src, tests, README (recurring.csv mentions stay) | "get rid of the old CSV stuff" |
+| 7 | `TALLY_FILE` override still works; README updated (`.json` example) | existing feature |
+
+---
+
+## Evaluation & Acceptance
+
+### Verification Command
+```bash
+python3 -m pytest -q
+grep -rniE "csv" src tests README.md   # only recurring.* hits allowed
+```
+
+---
+
+## Approach
+
+**Pattern reference**: `src/tally/storage.py` (keep `data_path`, `load`, `append`, `save_all`, `StorageError` signatures).
+**Vital slice**: storage.py + models (dict conversion replacing row conversion) + tests + README.
+**Cut list**: no CSV→JSON migration tool; no schema version field; no recurring.csv change.
+
